module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.StalkFreeCover
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FiniteTypeExtension

/-!
# Sections of a finite free sheaf of modules, and finite type without sheafification

Stacks 03DL defines a sheaf of modules on a ringed site to be *of finite type* when every object
of the site has a covering on whose members the sheaf is generated by finitely many sections,
"generated" meaning that every section over an object is, locally on a covering sieve, an
`R(W)`-linear combination of the restrictions of the chosen family. That is a condition on
*sections only*: it mentions neither the free sheaf of modules nor sheafification. Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, by contrast, asks for an epimorphism `free I ⟶ M|_U` out of a
finite free sheaf of modules, hence refers to a coproduct and — through the abelian structure of
`SheafOfModules` — to sheafification.

This file proves the two conditions **agree**, over an arbitrary site and with the ring and
module universes independent of the site universes.

One direction was already available: a generating family in the section sense induces a locally
surjective, hence epimorphic, map out of the free sheaf, because the free sheaf's tautological
sections *construct* the required local combinations. The direction that was missing is the
other one, and it is the content of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_eq_sum_smul_freeSection`: **for finite `I`, every section of
`SheafOfModules.free I` over an object is an `R`-linear combination of the tautological sections
`SheafOfModules.freeSection i`.** Without it, an epimorphism `free I ⟶ M|_U` gives only that
every section of `M` is locally the image of *some* section of `free I`, with no way to read
that section as a tuple of coefficients, and so yields no generating family in the section
sense.

The decomposition itself is obtained from the finite-biproduct coordinates
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeProj`, `freeCoord`, `freeMk` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.StalkFreeCover`, where the identity
`𝟙 (free I) = ∑ i, freeProj i ≫ ιFree i` is already proved; what is added here is the
identification of `(ιFree i).val.app V (unitOne V)` with `(freeSection i).eval V`, which is what
turns those coordinates into coefficients against the tautological sections.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.GeneratesLocally` is generation of a presheaf of modules over an object
  `U` by a finite family of sections of it over `U`: every section over an object of the site
  over `U` is, on a covering sieve, a linear combination of the restrictions of the family.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeSections` is the resulting sheafification-free finite type
  condition: some family of objects covering the site carries such a finite family.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relationsSubmodule` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relationsPresheaf` are
  the relations among a finite family of sections of `M` over `U`: over an object `V → U` of the
  slice site, the tuples of coefficients in `R(V)` whose linear combination of the restricted
  family vanishes, assembled into a presheaf of modules on the slice site.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_eq_sum_smul_freeSection`: **every section of a finite free sheaf
  of modules is a linear combination of the tautological sections.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_eq_sum_smul_freeHomEquiv`: the same statement pushed along a
  morphism `free I ⟶ N`, in equational and existential form. These are what a bare epimorphism
  out of a finite free sheaf of modules is worth on sections.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesLocally_of_epi`: **an epimorphism `free I ⟶ M|_U` out of a
  finite free sheaf of modules exhibits `M` as generated over `U`, in the section sense, by the
  images of the tautological sections.** Local surjectivity of an epimorphism
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi`) produces a covering sieve of the
  slice object `V → U` on which a given section lifts to the free sheaf; `Sieve.overEquiv`
  transports that sieve to the base, and the decomposition above turns the lift into
  coefficients.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_mkOver`: the converse construction, a generating
  family in the section sense induces an epimorphism out of the free sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeSections_of_isFiniteType` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeSections`: **the two finite type conditions
  agree.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesLocally_of_app_surjective`,
  `isFiniteTypeSections_of_app_surjective` and `isFiniteTypeSections_of_iso`: the
  sheafification-free condition is carried along a morphism surjective on all sections, hence is
  an isomorphism invariant.

## Implementation notes

**Which universes are independent.** The site is `C : Type u` with `Category.{v} C`, the sheaf of
rings is `R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}` and the sheaves of modules are `SheafOfModules.{t} R`: three
independent universes. That the module universe equals the ring universe is forced, not chosen —
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, `LocalGeneratorsData` and `IsFiniteType` are declared in
Mathlib only for `M : SheafOfModules.{t} R` with `R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}`, so there is no notion
of finite type for a sheaf of modules whose sections live in another universe. The *presheaf*-level
declarations `GeneratesLocally`, `IsFiniteTypeSections`, `relationsSubmodule` and
`relationsPresheaf` keep the module universe `m` and the index universe free, since they never
touch that API; `relationsPresheaf` lands in `PresheafOfModules.{max t i}` for an index type in
`Type i`, which is `PresheafOfModules.{t}` both for `I = Fin n` and for `I : Type t`.

**Which index universe.** `GeneratesLocally` takes an arbitrary finite index type rather than
`Fin n`, because the two consumers want different ones: the sheafification-free finite type
condition counts generators, so it wants `Fin n`, while `SheafOfModules.free I` needs `I : Type t`.
At `I = Fin n` with the standard `Fintype (Fin n)` instance the predicate is literally the `Fin n`
one, and `generatesLocally_comp_equiv` moves between index types.

**Which sheafification hypotheses.** Only the *slice* ones, `HasSheafify (J.over X)` and
`(J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective` for every object `X`, are assumed in the bridge section: the
free sheaf of modules, the epimorphism and the kernel all live on a slice site, and the base-site
instances are not needed. The decomposition section assumes only `HasWeakSheafify J`, which is
what `SheafOfModules.free` itself needs.

**`relationsPresheaf` is stated with coefficients in `R(V.left)`,** matching the source's
sectionwise kernel of `R(V)^I → M(V)`. Its restriction maps must then be written with an explicit
`ModuleCat.restrictScalars` wrapper, and the type of an element of the kernel must be ascribed in
the `toFun` field, because the elaborator will not otherwise reduce the object field far enough to
see that an element of it is a subtype. This is the same transparency obstruction that
`StalkFreeCover` records: `(R.over U).obj.obj (op V)` and `R.obj.obj (op V.left)` are
definitionally equal but not interchangeable for `rw` or for instance synthesis, which is why that
file carries two layers of coordinates.

**That second layer is not confined to the site of opens of a space**: the
whole `ofCoords`/`coords` development in `StalkFreeCover` has a general-site form under the
same names, together with an `Over U`-indexed layer (`ofCoordsOver`, `coordsOver`), which is the
form `relationsPresheaf` needs because it quantifies over a general `V : Over U` rather than over
`Over.mk f`. The sectionwise identification is then carried out over an arbitrary site in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.RelationsKernel`, whose
`bijOn_coordsOver_kernel` says that taking coordinates is a bijection from the sections of
`kernel (freeToOver M s)` over any `V : Over U` onto `relationsSubmodule M.val s V`.

The reason that result is phrased as a bijection on sections rather than as an isomorphism of
presheaves was the scalar **action**: for `a : R(V.left)` and `e` a section of `free I` over `V`,
`a • e` has no `HSMul` instance, because synthesis will not unfold `(R.over U).obj.obj (op V)` to
`R.obj.obj (op V.left)`.

**This is resolved, and the obstruction is narrower than it first appears.** It is
purely an instance-*synthesis* failure: where both types are already fixed the crossing is
definitional at default transparency, which is why `relationsPresheaf` could be defined at all.
So no bespoke surgery is needed — Mathlib's `PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars` along the
*identity* morphism of ring presheaves supplies it in a few lines, as `overBase` in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceScalarRestriction`. It changes only the
carrier's spelling, so exactly one `Module` instance is ever found; it must be a `def` with an
ascribed type rather than an `abbrev`, which instance search would unfold.

The isomorphism this passage called unavailable is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relationsPresheafIso`
in that file, and with it both directions of the finite-type agreement
(`isFiniteTypeSections_relationsPresheaf` and `isFiniteType_kernel_of_isFiniteTypeSections`) —
the second half of Tag 03DL's coherence condition, over an arbitrary site at the same three
independent universes used here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite SheafOfModules

universe t v u m i

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

section Decomposition

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{t}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{t}]

/-- The value over an object of the tautological section of a free sheaf of modules indexed by
`i` is the image of the unit section under the `i`-th summand inclusion. -/
lemma freeSection_eval {I : Type t} (i : I) (V : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (freeSection (R := R) i).eval V = (ιFree (R := R) i).val.app V (unitOne V) := by
  rw [show (freeSection (R := R) i).eval V
      = ((free (R := R) I).unitHomEquiv.symm (freeSection (R := R) i)).val.app V (unitOne V) from
        (unitHomEquiv_symm_app_unitOne _ V).symm,
    show (free (R := R) I).unitHomEquiv.symm (freeSection (R := R) i) = ιFree i from
      (unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply (𝟙 (free (R := R) I)) i).trans (Category.comp_id _)]

/-- **Every section of a finite free sheaf of modules is a linear combination of the
tautological sections.** -/
theorem exists_eq_sum_smul_freeSection {I : Type t} [Fintype I] (V : Cᵒᵖ)
    (e : ToType ((free (R := R) I).val.obj V)) :
    ∃ a : I → ToType (R.obj.obj V),
      ∑ i, a i • (freeSection (R := R) i).eval V = e := by
  classical
  refine ⟨freeCoord (S := R) V e, Eq.trans ?_ (freeMk_freeCoord (S := R) V e)⟩
  rw [freeMk]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [app_unit_eq, freeSection_eval]

/-- The image of the unit section under the `i`-th summand inclusion followed by a morphism out
of the free sheaf of modules is the `i`-th member of the corresponding family of sections. -/
lemma app_unitOne_ιFree_comp {N : SheafOfModules.{t} R} {I : Type t} (p : free I ⟶ N)
    (i : I) (V : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (ιFree (R := R) i ≫ p).val.app V (unitOne V) = (N.freeHomEquiv p i).eval V := by
  rw [← unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply, unitHomEquiv_symm_app_unitOne]

/-- **The coordinate formula for a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules**: on sections,
the morphism is the linear combination of the images of the tautological sections with the
coordinates of the argument as coefficients. -/
theorem app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord {N : SheafOfModules.{t} R} {I : Type t} [Fintype I]
    [DecidableEq I] (p : free I ⟶ N) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (e : ToType ((free (R := R) I).val.obj V)) :
    p.val.app V e = ∑ i, freeCoord (S := R) V e i • (N.freeHomEquiv p i).eval V := by
  have h := app_freeMk p V (freeCoord (S := R) V e)
  rw [freeMk_freeCoord] at h
  exact h.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [app_unitOne_ιFree_comp])

/-- **Every section of the image of a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules is a linear
combination of the images of the tautological sections.** -/
theorem exists_eq_sum_smul_freeHomEquiv {N : SheafOfModules.{t} R} {I : Type t} [Fintype I]
    (p : free I ⟶ N) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (e : ToType ((free (R := R) I).val.obj V)) :
    ∃ a : I → ToType (R.obj.obj V),
      ∑ i, a i • (N.freeHomEquiv p i).eval V = p.val.app V e := by
  classical
  exact ⟨freeCoord (S := R) V e, (app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord p V e).symm⟩

end Decomposition

/-! ### Local generation by a finite family of sections -/

section Generates

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}}

/-- A finite family of sections of a presheaf of modules over `U` **generates** it if every
section over an object of the site over `U` is, locally on a covering sieve, an `R(W)`-linear
combination of the restrictions of the family. -/
def GeneratesLocally (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R)
    {U : C} {I : Type*} [Fintype I] (s : I → M.obj (op U)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : C) (f : V ⟶ U) (t : M.obj (op V)),
    ∃ S : Sieve V, S ∈ J V ∧ ∀ (W : C) (g : W ⟶ V), S g →
      ∃ a : I → R.obj (op W),
        ∑ i, a i • M.restrictₛₗ (g ≫ f).op (s i) = M.restrictₛₗ g.op t

/-- Local generation is unchanged by reindexing the family along a bijection. -/
theorem generatesLocally_comp_equiv {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R}
    {U : C} {I I' : Type*} [Fintype I] [Fintype I'] (e : I' ≃ I) (s : I → M.obj (op U))
    (hs : GeneratesLocally J M s) : GeneratesLocally J M (s ∘ e) := by
  intro V f t
  obtain ⟨S, hS, h⟩ := hs V f t
  refine ⟨S, hS, fun W g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h W g hg
  exact ⟨a ∘ e, ha ▸ (Fintype.sum_equiv e _ _ fun _ => rfl)⟩

/-- A presheaf of modules is **of finite type** if some family of objects covering the site
carries a finite generating family of sections. This is the sheafification-free form of finite
type: it mentions neither kernels nor the free sheaf of modules. -/
class IsFiniteTypeSections (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop where
  /-- A covering family with finitely many local generators on each member. -/
  exists_generators : ∃ (I : Type u) (U : I → C), J.CoversTop U ∧
    ∀ i, ∃ (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → M.obj (op (U i))), GeneratesLocally J M s

/-- Local generation is carried along a morphism which is surjective on all sections. -/
theorem generatesLocally_of_app_surjective {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {M N : PresheafOfModules.{m} R} (ψ : M ⟶ N) (hψ : ∀ X, Function.Surjective (ψ.app X))
    {U : C} {I : Type*} [Fintype I] (s : I → M.obj (op U)) (hs : GeneratesLocally J M s) :
    GeneratesLocally J N (fun i => ψ.app (op U) (s i)) := by
  intro V f t
  obtain ⟨t', ht'⟩ := hψ (op V) t
  obtain ⟨S, hS, h⟩ := hs V f t'
  refine ⟨S, hS, fun W g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h W g hg
  refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
  calc ∑ i, a i • N.restrictₛₗ (g ≫ f).op (ψ.app (op U) (s i))
      = ψ.app (op W) (∑ i, a i • M.restrictₛₗ (g ≫ f).op (s i)) := by
        rw [map_sum]
        refine (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_).symm
        rw [map_smul]
        exact congrArg (a i • ·) (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ψ (g ≫ f).op (s i))
    _ = ψ.app (op W) (M.restrictₛₗ g.op t') := by rw [ha]
    _ = N.restrictₛₗ g.op t :=
        (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ψ g.op t').trans (congrArg (N.map g.op) ht')

/-- Finite type in the sheafification-free sense is carried along a morphism which is surjective
on all sections. -/
theorem isFiniteTypeSections_of_app_surjective {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {M N : PresheafOfModules.{m} R} (ψ : M ⟶ N) (hψ : ∀ X, Function.Surjective (ψ.app X))
    [IsFiniteTypeSections J M] : IsFiniteTypeSections J N := by
  obtain ⟨I, U, hU, hgen⟩ := IsFiniteTypeSections.exists_generators (J := J) (M := M)
  refine ⟨I, U, hU, fun i => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨n, s, hs⟩ := hgen i
  exact ⟨n, _, generatesLocally_of_app_surjective ψ hψ s hs⟩

/-- An isomorphism of presheaves of modules is surjective on all sections. -/
theorem surjective_app_of_iso {M N : PresheafOfModules.{m} R} (e : M ≅ N) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Surjective (e.hom.app X) := fun y =>
  ⟨e.inv.app X y, congrArg (fun ψ : N ⟶ N => ψ.app X y) e.inv_hom_id⟩

/-- Finite type in the sheafification-free sense is an isomorphism invariant. -/
theorem isFiniteTypeSections_of_iso {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {M N : PresheafOfModules.{m} R} (e : M ≅ N) [IsFiniteTypeSections J M] :
    IsFiniteTypeSections J N :=
  isFiniteTypeSections_of_app_surjective e.hom (surjective_app_of_iso e)

end Generates

/-! ### The presheaf of relations among a finite family of sections -/

section Relations

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}}

/-- The submodule of relations among a finite family of sections of `M` over `U`, read over an
object `V` of the slice site: the tuples of coefficients in `R(V)` whose linear combination of
the restrictions of the family vanishes. -/
noncomputable abbrev relationsSubmodule (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) {U : C} {I : Type i}
    [Fintype I] (s : I → M.obj (op U)) (V : Over U) :
    Submodule (R.obj (op V.left)) (I → R.obj (op V.left)) :=
  LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination (R.obj (op V.left))
    (fun i => M.restrictₛₗ V.hom.op (s i)))

/-- **The presheaf of relations among a finite family of sections of `M` over `U`.** Over an
object `V → U` of the slice site it is the kernel of `R(V)^I → M(V)` given by the restricted
family. No sheafification is involved. -/
noncomputable def relationsPresheaf (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) {U : C} {I : Type i}
    [Fintype I] (s : I → M.obj (op U)) :
    PresheafOfModules.{max t i} ((Over.forget U).op ⋙ R) where
  obj V := ModuleCat.of _ (relationsSubmodule M s V.unop)
  map {V W} f := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Y := (ModuleCat.restrictScalars (R.map f.unop.left.op).hom).obj
      (ModuleCat.of _ (relationsSubmodule M s W.unop)))
    { toFun := fun a : relationsSubmodule M s V.unop =>
        ⟨fun i => R.map f.unop.left.op (a.val i), by
          have h := congrArg (M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op) a.property
          change (∑ i, R.map f.unop.left.op (a.val i) •
            M.restrictₛₗ W.unop.hom.op (s i)) = 0
          change M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op
            (∑ i, a.val i • M.restrictₛₗ V.unop.hom.op (s i))
              = M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op 0 at h
          have hc (i : I) :
              M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op (M.restrictₛₗ V.unop.hom.op (s i)) =
                M.restrictₛₗ W.unop.hom.op (s i) :=
            (M.map_comp_apply _ _ _).symm.trans
              (M.congr_map_apply (congrArg Quiver.Hom.op (Over.w f.unop)) _)
          simpa only [map_sum, map_smulₛₗ, hc, map_zero] using h⟩
      map_add' := by intro a b; apply Subtype.ext; funext i; exact map_add _ _ _
      map_smul' := by intro r a; apply Subtype.ext; funext i; exact map_mul _ _ _ }
  map_id V := by
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun a => Subtype.ext (funext fun i => ?_))
    exact congrArg (fun φ => φ (a.val i)) (R.map_id _)
  map_comp f g := by
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun a => Subtype.ext (funext fun i => ?_))
    exact congrArg (fun φ => φ (a.val i)) (R.map_comp f.unop.left.op g.unop.left.op)

end Relations

/-! ### Mathlib's finite type implies local generation -/

section Bridge

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}}
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{t}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{t}]

/-- **An epimorphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules onto a restriction `M|_U` exhibits
`M` as locally generated over `U` by the images of the tautological sections.** -/
theorem generatesLocally_of_epi {M : SheafOfModules.{t} R} (U : C) {I : Type t} [Fintype I]
    (p : free (R := R.over U) I ⟶ M.over U) [Epi p] :
    GeneratesLocally J M.val (fun i => evalOver ((M.over U).freeHomEquiv p i)) := by
  intro V f t
  obtain ⟨S', hS', hsec⟩ := EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi p (V := Over.mk f) t
  refine ⟨Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk f) S', (J.mem_over_iff _).mp hS', fun W g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hsec (Over.homMk g : Over.mk (g ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk f)
    ((Sieve.overEquiv_iff _ _).mp hg)
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_eq_sum_smul_freeHomEquiv p (op (Over.mk (g ≫ f))) e
  have h1 : ∀ i, ((M.over U).freeHomEquiv p i).eval (op (Over.mk (g ≫ f)))
      = (M.over U).val.map (Over.homMk (g ≫ f) (Category.comp_id _) :
            Over.mk (g ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 U)).op
          (evalOver ((M.over U).freeHomEquiv p i)) := fun i =>
    (PresheafOfModules.sections_property ((M.over U).freeHomEquiv p i)
      (Over.homMk (g ≫ f) (Category.comp_id _) :
        Over.mk (g ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 U)).op).symm
  exact ⟨fun i => a i,
    ((Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => congrArg (a i • ·) (h1 i)).symm.trans ha).trans he⟩

/-- **A finite generating family in the sheafification-free sense induces an epimorphism from
the finite free sheaf of modules on the slice site.** -/
theorem epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_mkOver {M : SheafOfModules.{t} R} {U : C} {I : Type t} [Fintype I]
    (s : I → M.val.obj (op U)) (hs : GeneratesLocally J M.val s) :
    Epi ((M.over U).freeHomEquiv.symm (fun i => mkOver (M := M) (V := U) (s i))) := by
  classical
  set p := (M.over U).freeHomEquiv.symm (fun i => mkOver (M := M) (V := U) (s i)) with hp
  have hgen : ∀ (i : I) (Z : Over U),
      (ιFree (R := R.over U) i ≫ p).val.app (op Z) (unitOne (op Z))
        = (mkOver (M := M) (V := U) (s i)).eval (op Z) := fun i Z => by
    rw [app_unitOne_ιFree_comp, hp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  refine EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective p ⟨fun {Z} tz => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨T, hT, ht⟩ := hs Z.left Z.hom tz
  refine (J.over U).superset_covering ?_ (J.overEquiv_symm_mem_over Z T hT)
  intro W f hf
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := ht W.left f.left hf
  have hw : ∀ i, M.val.restrictₛₗ (f.left ≫ Z.hom).op (s i) = M.val.map W.hom.op (s i) :=
    fun i => M.val.congr_map_apply (congrArg Quiver.Hom.op (Over.w f)) _
  exact ⟨freeMk (S := R.over U) (op W) a, (app_freeMk p (op W) a).trans
    ((Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => congrArg _ ((hgen i W).trans (hw i).symm)).trans ha)⟩

/-- **Mathlib's finite type condition implies the sheafification-free one.** -/
theorem isFiniteTypeSections_of_isFiniteType (M : SheafOfModules.{t} R) [M.IsFiniteType] :
    IsFiniteTypeSections J M.val := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  refine ⟨σ.I, σ.X, σ.coversTop, fun i => ?_⟩
  have := (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
  cases nonempty_fintype (σ.generators i).I
  exact ⟨Fintype.card (σ.generators i).I, _,
    generatesLocally_comp_equiv (Fintype.equivFin _).symm _
      (generatesLocally_of_epi (σ.X i) (σ.generators i).π)⟩

/-- **The sheafification-free finite type condition implies Mathlib's.** Together with
`isFiniteTypeSections_of_isFiniteType` this says the two notions agree. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeSections (M : SheafOfModules.{t} R)
    [IsFiniteTypeSections J M.val] : M.IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨I, U, hU, hgen⟩ := IsFiniteTypeSections.exists_generators (J := J) (M := M.val)
  choose n s hs using hgen
  refine ⟨⟨{ I := I
             X := U
             coversTop := hU
             generators := fun i =>
               { I := ULift.{t} (Fin (n i))
                 s := fun j => mkOver (s i j.down)
                 epi := epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_mkOver _
                   (generatesLocally_comp_equiv Equiv.ulift (s i) (hs i)) } },
    ⟨fun i => ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite (ULift.{t} (Fin (n i))))⟩⟩⟩⟩

end Bridge

